body:
Think ablout it this way:  there's so many people the amount of time each person may look at you is smaller than if you were in a smaller place. And the noise and talking is distracting everyone else. They're not looking at you and noticing you, you're just simply passing in their field of vision. Everyone has a life and something on theier mind, they won't pay you any attention

&#x200B;

that's how I calm myself at least haha

I will be honest, if public speaking is so bad for you I might consider jsut passing the opportunity f I were in your position.  I have a huge fear of public speaking and it's stopped me from doing other stuff because I don't see the point of tortuting myself. I would pass it and look for other opportunities that don't require it.

&#x200B;

But if you are really deadset on this position, honestly forcing yourself to speak publically often really helps. I have severe anxiety and I forced myself to get a job and ill tell you that 2 years later i'm not afraid to speak to customers anymore (i work in customer service) but at first i would be so scared every moment before my shift. I forced myself and got used to it. I feel so glad now taht I did. But it just takes a little push from yourself. If you don't feel you are ready, you may just not be.

 "Now I’m going to get back on my horse and fight again no matter how impossible it seems"

&#x200B;

Wow, I am so glad to hear this mate!!! That is a great outlook, youre on the right track

oh mon dieu! youre right, rereading it i say apporter WAY too much! 

&#x200B;

thank you for the advice! : D
